# Degree-five natural-plus-dual actors

This interface exposes the actual automorphism group, its inner subgroup,
the marked radical, outer-involution conjugators and centralizers, and
the complete outer fixed-module decomposition, exhaustive high-rank actor
classification, radical hyperplane formulas and full generated cores.
Every conjugator and subspace is attached to the actual action. The module
statements take the natural-plus-dual coordinate representation explicitly;
its construction and arbitrary-source-module comparison remain with H.9.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), H.9.2,
printed pp.390–391 (PDF pp.401–402).
-/
